# update-expected.py's M23 additions (plan 5.12.4): with the stand-in
# compiler of lit.local.cfg,
# (1) Inputs/ue/corpus-copts.test takes a source from %{msil_corpus}, which
#     is --corpus-dir (a fake cache with src/lib.c), adds its %{msil_copts}
#     to the native build and writes the transcript to the file its
#     %{msil_expect} names (corpus-shared.expected; no
#     corpus-copts.expected); --check then matches it;
# (2) a directory with libc-free.txt (c-testsuite's lit test format) is
#     skipped as a whole, and a directory whose lit.local.cfg sets
#     config.suffixes = [".test"] (msil/test/Programs) contributes no .c
#     file, in its subdirectories neither, so its drivers are not reported;
# (3) Inputs/ue/no-parts.test has no split-file parts and names its sources
#     in its own directory (%S), as msil/test/Programs does: it is built
#     natively without split-file, so its .expected is written and checked
#     also when --split-file is a stand-in that fails (an unknown mode of
#     the stand-in), which a test with parts (corpus-copts.test) does run;
# (4) a single-source test whose %{msil_copts} has an unterminated quote
#     (Inputs/ue/bad-copts.c) is an error that names the test and the quote,
#     with no native build, no .expected and exit status 1, as for a
#     %{msil_prog} test;
# (5) a directory below a .test-only one contributes no .c file also when
#     the walk starts there (msil/test/Programs/support, whose
#     lit.local.cfg is msil/test/Programs'), and a tuple (".test",) makes a
#     directory .test-only as the list does.
# RUN: rm -rf %t.d %t.corpus %t.walk && mkdir -p %t.d %t.corpus/src %t.walk/ctest %t.walk/progs/sub %t.walk/progs2
# RUN: cat %S/Inputs/ue/corpus-copts.test > %t.d/corpus-copts.test
# RUN: %{harness_check} write %t.corpus/src/lib.c "// prog-value: 9"

